253
00:15:14,440 --> 00:15:18,577
Chris Height, you're obviously
well-connected, and with a little digging,

254
00:15:18,660 --> 00:15:22,517
you could find out what the real-life
name and address of this death gun is.

255
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:26,537
Just make a list of the handles of all
the surviving Laughing Coffin members,

256
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:28,180
then contact their ISPs,

257
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:32,012
ask which one's playing GGO
now, and trace their location.

258
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:34,064
No, sorry, that's not possible.

259
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:36,637
The ISPs aren't going to
give out a player's real

260
00:15:36,720 --> 00:15:39,757
-life info if all we have
to go on are their handles.

261
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:42,437
Maybe if we ask the game's
admins, they could help.

262
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:45,277
They might, but GGO's
admins are in the U .S.,

263
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:47,948
so it'll be a while
before we got an answer.

264
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:54,140
I know my brother, and right now
he's risking his life in that game,

265
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:56,675
trying to find out who this person is.

266
00:15:56,800 --> 00:16:01,682
When he came home last night, he had this
look on his face, like he'd seen a ghost.

267
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:05,647
He must have bumped into the guy
yesterday during the prelims.

268
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:10,300
I bet that's when he realized someone
from Laughing Coffin was in GGO.

269
00:16:11,380 --> 00:16:14,851
Someone who figured out how to
kill players for real again.

270
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:18,618
My brother went back to put
an end to that nightmare.

271
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:22,600
To find out his name and stop
his PK-ing once and for all.

272
00:16:23,780 --> 00:16:24,897
Darn it, Kirito!

273
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:26,804
You should have said something?

274
00:16:27,500 --> 00:16:28,330
Why?

275
00:16:28,413 --> 00:16:30,040
Why do you always do this?

276
00:16:30,940 --> 00:16:34,220
That damn idiot Why
didn't he say anything?

277
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:36,357
I could be backing him up right now.

278
00:16:36,440 --> 00:16:39,677
All he had to do was ask and I
would have converted over too!

279
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:40,917
We all would have.

280
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:41,840
Don't you see?

281
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,537
That's why he didn't tell us.

282
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:46,737
If he thought there was any real
danger in what he was doing,

283
00:16:46,820 --> 00:16:49,357
there's no way he'd get
us mixed up in it, too.

284
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:50,760
That's just how he is.

285
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:52,537
Yeah, you're right.

286
00:16:52,620 --> 00:16:55,091
He always thinks of others before himself.

287
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:57,757
In fact, he's probably
protecting someone right now.

288
00:16:57,840 --> 00:17:01,722
And whoever that is, I bet it's
someone who doesn't like him much.

289
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:09,200
Okay, Chris Head Where
is Kirito diving from?

290
00:17:09,460 --> 00:17:11,989
I know you know, so
you better tell me now?

291
00:17:13,740 --> 00:17:14,916
That's confidential.

292
00:17:16,880 --> 00:17:17,710
Okay, okay.

293
00:17:17,793 --> 00:17:18,837
I'll tell you.

294
00:17:18,920 --> 00:17:21,397
I set up the room myself, so he's safe.

295
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:22,797
Security's rock solid.

296
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:24,457
And the monitoring's top of the line.

297
00:17:24,540 --> 00:17:27,817
I've got a trained professional
right by his side at all times.

298
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:30,597
And I guarantee that his
body's in no danger whatsoever.

299
00:17:30,680 --> 00:17:31,620
Where is he?

300
00:17:33,000 --> 00:17:33,877
A hospital.

301
00:17:33,960 --> 00:17:37,320
It's in Ocha no Miss, in
Chiyoda ward. He's in Chiyoda?

302
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:41,457
Wait, is that the same hospital he
was in during his rehabilitation?

303
00:17:41,540 --> 00:17:43,020
Yes, that's the one.

304
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,677
I'm going over there.

305
00:17:44,760 --> 00:17:47,878
I want to see him, and you
can't do a thing about it.

306
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:55,940
Tell me you got a plan.

307
00:17:57,320 --> 00:17:59,320
We're going to take out Death Gun.

308
00:17:59,700 --> 00:18:03,020
Once we do, his real-world
partner will stand down.

309
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:05,696
Then he'll just leave your apartment.

310
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:07,640
Okay, but he's skilled.

311
00:18:08,140 --> 00:18:09,840
Black star or no black star.

312
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:14,740
You saw he dodged Hecate's
bullet from just 100 meters away.

313
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:19,740
And besides, I can't hide in
this cave forever, you know?

314
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:24,157
By now, the other players probably
figured out the two of us are in here.

315
00:18:24,240 --> 00:18:26,240
We might as well be sitting ducks.

316
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:29,917
It's just a matter of time before
someone tosses a grenade in.

317
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:30,830
You're right.

318
00:18:31,220 --> 00:18:34,044
We've been a team this
whole time anyway, right?

319
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:36,401
Might as well finish it together.

320
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:40,548
Okay, but there's still the risk
he shoots you with that gun.

321
00:18:41,020 --> 00:18:41,940
Oh, that thing?

322
00:18:42,220 --> 00:18:44,926
It's just an old-school
single-action sidearm.

323
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:48,060
He can fire it all he
wants, but I got you there.

324
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:50,497
Just deflect the bullets with your sword.

325
00:18:50,580 --> 00:18:53,639
Right, and I won't let a
single one of them hit you.

326
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:56,837
I still don't feel good about
you being out there, though.

327
00:18:56,920 --> 00:19:00,317
I mean, Death Gun's dangerous, and
you shouldn't get too close to him.

328
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:02,260
Oh, come on. Hang on.

329
00:19:02,520 --> 00:19:06,537
I'm totally cool with you fighting with
me, and I wouldn't have it any other way.

330
00:19:06,620 --> 00:19:09,080
But Sinon, you're a sniper, remember?

331
00:19:09,480 --> 00:19:11,917
Isn't your specialty
the long-range attack?

332
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,780
Well, yeah. What about it?

333
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:15,321
Here's the plan.

334
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:18,797
On the next scan, I'm going to
step outside so it picks me up.

335
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:21,468
That way, we'll get
Death Gun to come to us.

336
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:23,877
He'll probably keep his
distance and take cover.

337
00:19:23,960 --> 00:19:26,577
Then he'll try to pick
me off with his rifle.

338
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:30,137
When he shoots, we'll know where
he is, and then you take him out.

339
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:31,279
What do you think?

340
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:34,280
Are you cool with playing
the decoy? Mm-hmm.

341
00:19:35,380 --> 00:19:37,420
All right, we do it your way then.

342
00:19:37,860 --> 00:19:39,257
Just be careful out there,

343
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:43,340
because if he drops you with his
first shot, I'm going to be pissed.

344
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:45,073
I'll keep that in mind.

345
00:19:45,720 --> 00:19:47,057
Wait, I just remembered.

346
00:19:47,140 --> 00:19:51,197
His rifle's got a silencer, and you won't
see the bullet line on the first shot.

347
00:19:51,280 --> 00:19:53,437
Oh, I'll just predict the prediction.

348
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:56,226
You know, like a certain
no-good faker told...

349
00:19:57,180 --> 00:19:59,400
Um, I think we should stop talking.

350
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:05,517
Oh, crap.

351
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:07,837
We should have been paying more attention.

352
00:20:07,920 --> 00:20:08,840
What is it?

353
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:10,700
And will it kill us?

354
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,560
It's a live stream camera.

355
00:20:13,080 --> 00:20:15,897
Usually, they're only supposed to
shadow players on the battlefield.

356
00:20:15,980 --> 00:20:16,810
field.

357
00:20:16,893 --> 00:20:20,357
I guess this one's in here now, because
there aren't many of us left out there.

358
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:23,320
Then, do you think it hurt us?

359
00:20:23,620 --> 00:20:24,660
Not a chance.

360
00:20:24,940 --> 00:20:28,337
For it to pick us up, we'd have to
be shouting at the top of our lungs.

361
00:20:28,420 --> 00:20:29,660
Wave to the audience.

362
00:20:30,580 --> 00:20:32,756
Unless, you got someone back at home.

363
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:34,428
You don't want seeing this.

364
00:20:36,660 --> 00:20:37,540
I, um...

365
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:40,577
Shouldn't you be worried who's watching?

366
00:20:40,660 --> 00:20:43,857
I mean, since I sort of look like
a girl, they might, you know,

367
00:20:43,940 --> 00:20:45,317
think you're, you know...

368
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:47,200
Well, I don't care.

369
00:20:47,320 --> 00:20:48,717
They can think what they want.

370
00:20:48,800 --> 00:20:50,337
The guys in this game are dorks.

371
00:20:50,420 --> 00:20:54,217
If they think I'm gay, at least they'll
stop hitting on me every five seconds.

372
00:20:54,300 --> 00:20:57,437
How much longer am I going to have
to keep pretending to be a girl?

373
00:20:57,520 --> 00:20:58,880
Oh, you poor baby.

374
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:01,477
You've been faking it like
a champ since you logged in.

375
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:03,501
Another hour or two won't matter.

376
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:05,030
Thank God.

377
00:21:07,860 --> 00:21:09,120
We better get ready.

378
00:21:10,260 --> 00:21:12,848
We got two minutes
before the next SAT scan.

379
00:21:13,380 --> 00:21:14,380
I'll set up here.

380
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:19,325
When you get outside, fire up your terminal
and let me know when our boy's close.

381
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:24,540
Wait. Hold on.

382
00:21:25,060 --> 00:21:26,320
Why? What's wrong?

383
00:21:26,760 --> 00:21:28,936
It's too late to change the plan now.

384
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:30,270
No.

385
00:21:30,353 --> 00:21:31,937
I don't want to change anything.

386
00:21:32,020 --> 00:21:33,200
It's something else.

387
00:21:33,580 --> 00:21:36,815
I was just thinking about
Death Gun's real handle here.

388
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:40,217
The only name you didn't recognize
who's still alive is Sterben.

389
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:41,360
Oh. Huh.

390
00:21:42,680 --> 00:21:43,797
Oh, I guess that's him, then.

391
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:46,645
I wonder why he gave
himself that name, though.

392
00:21:47,100 --> 00:21:50,865
If I get up close and personal,
I'll be sure to ask him for you.

393
00:21:52,860 --> 00:21:54,560
Well, here goes nothing.

394
00:21:57,420 --> 00:21:58,620
Be careful, okay?

395
00:22:11,360 --> 00:22:13,597
I'd like to pray for the pain.

396
00:22:13,680 --> 00:22:15,617
I've been in a

397
00:22:15,700 --> 00:22:22,700
long

398
00:22:25,260 --> 00:22:26,837
time.

399
00:22:26,920 --> 00:22:29,697
I've never been in a long time.

400
00:22:29,780 --> 00:22:33,297
I've never seen any of my pain.

401
00:22:33,380 --> 00:22:36,937
I've been hiding a long time.

402
00:22:37,020 --> 00:22:41,240
I've always been in a long time.

403
00:22:49,540 --> 00:22:51,500
Thank you.

404
00:23:35,660 --> 00:23:38,080
Next time, bullet of a phantom.

405
00:23:41,240 --> 00:23:42,070
You
